{"en":[{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"A <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/state\" title=\"state\">state</a> of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/balance\" title=\"balance\">balance</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/equilibrium\" title=\"equilibrium\">equilibrium</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/stability\" title=\"stability\">stability</a>."},{"definition":"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/composure\" title=\"composure\">Composure</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/freedom\" title=\"freedom\">freedom</a> from <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/embarrassment\" title=\"embarrassment\">embarrassment</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/affectation\" title=\"affectation\">affectation</a>."},{"definition":"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/mien\" title=\"mien\">Mien</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/bearing\" title=\"bearing\">bearing</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/deportment\" title=\"deportment\">deportment</a> of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/head\" title=\"head\">head</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/body\" title=\"body\">body</a>."},{"definition":"A <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/condition\" title=\"condition\">condition</a> of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/hover\" title=\"hover\">hovering</a>, or being <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/suspend\" title=\"suspend\">suspended</a>."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt17\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> A <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/CGS\" title=\"CGS\">CGS</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/unit\" title=\"unit\">unit</a> of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/dynamic\" title=\"dynamic\">dynamic</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/viscosity\" title=\"viscosity\">viscosity</a> equal to one <span class=\"new\">dyne-second</span> per <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/square_centimetre\" title=\"square centimetre\">square centimetre</a>."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt19\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/weight\" title=\"weight\">Weight</a>; an amount of weight, the amount something weighs."},{"definition":"The weight, or mass of metal, used in weighing, to balance the substance weighed."},{"definition":"That which causes a balance; a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/counterweight\" title=\"counterweight\">counterweight</a>."}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Verb","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt129\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> To hang in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/equilibrium\" title=\"equilibrium\">equilibrium</a>; to be balanced or suspended; hence, to be in suspense or doubt."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt131\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> To <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/counterpoise\" title=\"counterpoise\">counterpoise</a>; to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/counterbalance\" title=\"counterbalance\">counterbalance</a>."},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt134\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> To be of a given <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/weight\" title=\"weight\">weight</a>; to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/weigh\" title=\"weigh\">weigh</a>. <style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r90144991\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt135\">.mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}</style>"},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt137\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> To add weight to, to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/weigh_down\" title=\"weigh down\">weigh down</a>. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt138\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"<span class=\"usage-label-sense\" about=\"#mwt141\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"></span> To <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/hold\" title=\"hold\">hold</a> (something) <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\" about=\"#mwt142\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/with#English\" title=\"with\">with</a></i> or <i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"en\" about=\"#mwt143\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/against#English\" title=\"against\">against</a></i> something else in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/equilibrium\" title=\"equilibrium\">equilibrium</a>; to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/balance\" title=\"balance\">balance</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/counterpose\" title=\"counterpose\">counterpose</a>. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt144\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">"},{"definition":"To hold (something) in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/equilibrium\" title=\"equilibrium\">equilibrium</a>, to hold <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/balanced\" title=\"balanced\">balanced</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/ready\" title=\"ready\">ready</a>; to carry (something) ready to be used. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt147\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">","parsedExamples":[{"example":"I <b>poised</b> the crowbar in my hand, and waited."},{"example":"to <b>poise</b> the scales of a balance"}],"examples":["I <b>poised</b> the crowbar in my hand, and waited.","to <b>poise</b> the scales of a balance"]},{"definition":"To keep (something) in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/equilibrium\" title=\"equilibrium\">equilibrium</a>; to hold <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/suspended\" title=\"suspended\">suspended</a> or balanced. <link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r90144991\" about=\"#mwt153\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\">","parsedExamples":[{"example":"The rock was <b>poised</b> precariously on the edge of the cliff."}],"examples":["The rock was <b>poised</b> precariously on the edge of the cliff."]},{"definition":"To <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/ascertain\" title=\"ascertain\">ascertain</a>, as if by balancing; to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/weigh\" title=\"weigh\">weigh</a>."}]},{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"English","definitions":[{"definition":"Unit of viscosity in the centimetre–gram–second system of units (CGS)."}]}],"other":[{"partOfSpeech":"Noun","language":"Old French","definitions":[{"definition":"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/weight\" title=\"weight\">weight</a>"},{"definition":"a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/unit\" title=\"unit\">unit</a> of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/measure\" title=\"measure\">measure</a> of unknown value (which presumably varied because of the technology of the time)"}]}],"pt":[{"partOfSpeech":"Verb","language":"Portuguese","definitions":[{"definition":"<span class=\"form-of-definition use-with-mention\" about=\"#mwt188\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\">inflection of <span class=\"form-of-definition-link\"><i class=\"Latn mention\" lang=\"pt\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/poisar#Portuguese\" title=\"poisar\">poisar</a></i></span>:</span><span about=\"#mwt188\">\n</span><ol about=\"#mwt188\"><li><span class=\"form-of-definition use-with-mention\"><span class=\"inflection-of-conjoined\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#first_person\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">first</a><span class=\"inflection-of-sep\">/</span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#third_person\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">third-person</a></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#singular_number\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">singular</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#present_tense\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">present</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#subjunctive_mood\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">subjunctive</a></span></li>\n<li><span class=\"form-of-definition use-with-mention\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#third_person\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">third-person</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#singular_number\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">singular</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#imperative_mood\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">imperative</a></span></li></ol>"},{"definition":"<span class=\"form-of-definition use-with-mention\"><span class=\"inflection-of-conjoined\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#first_person\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">first</a><span class=\"inflection-of-sep\">/</span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#third_person\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">third-person</a></span> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#singular_number\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">singular</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#present_tense\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">present</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#subjunctive_mood\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">subjunctive</a></span>"},{"definition":"<span class=\"form-of-definition use-with-mention\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#third_person\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">third-person</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#singular_number\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">singular</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"/wiki/Appendix:Glossary#imperative_mood\" title=\"Appendix:Glossary\">imperative</a></span>"}]}]}